  "id": "rokeach-value-survey",
  "term": "Rokeach Value Survey",
  "definition": "The Rokeach Value Survey is a measure of human values that has been widely used in areas such as social psychology, work-related assessment, marketing, and cross-cultural research. In this source, it is described as an older values instrument whose items can be aligned with the Schwartz value framework so researchers can study values across datasets and over time.",
